# REQUIRES: verilator
# The kernel's static port (shell/rtl/foldsim_vport.sv) alone, against
# Inputs/tb_vport.sv: a memory that applies a write at its B and reads rows at
# AR (one id, in order), so a read that reached AR before the B of an earlier
# write of its row would answer the old row; answers checked against a
# reference RAM. Reads carry fence class 0 (every earlier write) or (+far)
# class 2 for rows not written within that distance; read-first pairs (the
# write waits for the reads taken up to its cycle). HBM latency 1 to 600
# memory cycles, channels stalled at random, resets with requests in flight
# (no pre-reset answer delivered, memory zero-filled before room returns), a
# reset of a region the host cleared (+clean: no fill); rows of three beats,
# one beat and 64 bits.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -DSIMULATION --top-module tb -GDW=1040 -GCYCLES=12000 -Mdir %t/wide %S/Inputs/tb_vport.sv %S/../../shell/rtl/foldsim_vport.sv > %t/wide.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/wide/Vtb +verilator+seed+1 +hi=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/wide/Vtb +verilator+seed+2 +hi=600 +stall=30 +cycles=30000 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/wide/Vtb +verilator+seed+3 +hi=60 +stall=20 +resets=3 | FileCheck %s
# The write queue under pressure (W held back, nearly every issue a write): a row's slot is free as the streamer
# takes it into its row stage, so the queue's next writes must not reach the row still on W.
# RUN: %t/wide/Vtb +verilator+seed+16 +hi=600 +stall=70 +wr=95 +cycles=30000 | FileCheck %s
# Fence class 2 at its least distance: reads of rows written exactly 3 * 2^FS host cycles before.
# RUN: %t/wide/Vtb +verilator+seed+17 +hi=40 +far=1 +edge=50 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -DSIMULATION --top-module tb -GDW=512 -GCYCLES=12000 -Mdir %t/beat %S/Inputs/tb_vport.sv %S/../../shell/rtl/foldsim_vport.sv > %t/beat.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/beat/Vtb +verilator+seed+4 +hi=100 +far=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/beat/Vtb +verilator+seed+5 +hi=600 +resets=4 +cycles=30000 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/beat/Vtb +verilator+seed+15 +hi=200 +stall=10 +resets=2 +clean=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -DSIMULATION --top-module tb -GDW=64 -GCYCLES=12000 -Mdir %t/narrow %S/Inputs/tb_vport.sv %S/../../shell/rtl/foldsim_vport.sv > %t/narrow.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/narrow/Vtb +verilator+seed+6 +hi=20 +far=1 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/narrow/Vtb +verilator+seed+7 +hi=600 +stall=10 +resets=2 +cycles=30000 | FileCheck %s
# A write-number table (HZ 3: 8 entries, so rows share them) in place of fence classes.
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -DSIMULATION --top-module tb -GDW=1040 -GHZ=3 -GCYCLES=12000 -Mdir %t/hz %S/Inputs/tb_vport.sv %S/../../shell/rtl/foldsim_vport.sv > %t/hz.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/hz/Vtb +verilator+seed+8 +hi=600 +stall=20 +resets=2 +cycles=30000 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/hz/Vtb +verilator+seed+9 +hi=40 | FileCheck %s
#
# Bursts (MAX_BURST 8) under AXI credit (4 reads / 4 writes in flight, checked
# never exceeded): 32 instances sweep their rows so that requests follow each
# other in memory; fewer ARs than reads (+merge) and fewer AWs than writes
# (+wmerge); no burst over 8 beats or across a 4 KiB page; ordering exact.
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -DSIMULATION --top-module tb -GIW=5 -GDW=512 -GCOPY=1 -GMAX_BURST=8 -GAXI_RD_OUT=4 -GAXI_WR_OUT=4 -GCYCLES=12000 -Mdir %t/merge %S/Inputs/tb_vport.sv %S/../../shell/rtl/foldsim_vport.sv > %t/merge.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/merge/Vtb +verilator+seed+10 +hi=200 +seq=90 +far=1 +wr=10 +merge=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/merge/Vtb +verilator+seed+11 +hi=600 +seq=98 +far=1 +wr=0 +merge=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/merge/Vtb +verilator+seed+12 +hi=600 +seq=99 +wr=100 +far=1 +wmerge=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/merge/Vtb +verilator+seed+13 +hi=60 +seq=70 +stall=10 +copy=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/merge/Vtb +verilator+seed+14 +hi=100 +seq=60 +stall=20 +resets=3 | FileCheck %s
# Write-first pairs whose read copies (rd_new + rd_copy): the copy slot goes after the write (else a deadlock).
# RUN: %t/merge/Vtb +verilator+seed+16 +hi=60 +copy=40 +wf=50 +stall=10 | FileCheck %s
#
# The AXI side in its own clock at 256 bits (ASYNC, as on the shell's direct
# HBM ports), clock ratios 2:1, 1:2, 2511:1777, 1:3 and 3:1, with ring copies
# (COPY: a read's beats into the port's write queue, answered once with
# rsp_copied; image reads with rd_after_copies see every earlier copy), bursts
# under 16 credits, an aligned base; resets with copies in flight (the
# unfilled ones are written with no byte enabled).
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -DSIMULATION --top-module tb -GIW=5 -GDW=512 -GASYNC=1 -GCOPY=1 -GMAX_BURST=8 -GAXI_RD_OUT=16 -GAXI_WR_OUT=16 -GBASE_ALIGNED=1 -GOUTSTANDING=32 -GWRITES_OUT=16 -GCYCLES=12000 -Mdir %t/async %S/Inputs/tb_vport.sv %S/../../shell/rtl/foldsim_vport.sv > %t/async.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/async/Vtb +verilator+seed+20 +sp=2500 +mp=1250 +hi=50 +copy=40 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/async/Vtb +verilator+seed+21 +sp=1250 +mp=2500 +hi=600 +copy=30 +stall=30 +cycles=30000 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/async/Vtb +verilator+seed+22 +sp=2511 +mp=1777 +hi=80 +copy=40 +stall=20 +resets=3 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/async/Vtb +verilator+seed+23 +sp=1000 +mp=3000 +hi=60 +copy=30 +seq=60 +stall=10 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/async/Vtb +verilator+seed+24 +sp=3000 +mp=1000 +hi=1 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/async/Vtb +verilator+seed+25 +sp=2500 +mp=1250 +hi=150 +copy=40 +resets=2 +clean=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/async/Vtb +verilator+seed+26 +sp=2511 +mp=1777 +hi=80 +copy=40 +wf=50 +stall=20 +resets=3 | FileCheck %s
# Three-beat rows, a write-number table, image reads at fence class 2 (only
# rd_after_copies orders them after the copies).
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -DSIMULATION --top-module tb -GDW=1040 -GASYNC=1 -GCOPY=1 -GHZ=3 -GCYCLES=12000 -Mdir %t/acopy %S/Inputs/tb_vport.sv %S/../../shell/rtl/foldsim_vport.sv > %t/acopy.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/acopy/Vtb +verilator+seed+30 +sp=2500 +mp=1250 +hi=80 +copy=40 +stall=20 +resets=3 +far=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/acopy/Vtb +verilator+seed+31 +sp=2511 +mp=1777 +hi=60 +copy=30 +seq=60 +stall=10 +far=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/acopy/Vtb +verilator+seed+32 +sp=1000 +mp=3000 +hi=600 +copy=30 +stall=30 +cycles=30000 | FileCheck %s
# The write number a read waits for handed in by its sender (NEED_IN: the
# driver keeps each row's newest number from w_count), with bursts and copies.
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -DSIMULATION --top-module tb -GDW=1040 -GNEED_IN=1 -GCYCLES=12000 -Mdir %t/need %S/Inputs/tb_vport.sv %S/../../shell/rtl/foldsim_vport.sv > %t/need.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/need/Vtb +verilator+seed+40 +hi=600 +stall=30 +cycles=30000 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/need/Vtb +verilator+seed+41 +hi=60 +stall=20 +resets=3 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -DSIMULATION --top-module tb -GIW=5 -GDW=512 -GASYNC=1 -GCOPY=1 -GMAX_BURST=8 -GAXI_RD_OUT=4 -GAXI_WR_OUT=4 -GNEED_IN=1 -GCYCLES=12000 -Mdir %t/needm %S/Inputs/tb_vport.sv %S/../../shell/rtl/foldsim_vport.sv > %t/needm.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/needm/Vtb +verilator+seed+42 +sp=2500 +mp=1250 +hi=60 +seq=70 +stall=10 +copy=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/needm/Vtb +verilator+seed+43 +sp=2511 +mp=1777 +hi=200 +seq=90 +wr=60 +resets=2 | FileCheck %s
# CHECK-NOT: FAIL
# CHECK-NOT: %Error
# CHECK: {{[0-9]+}} reads ({{[0-9]+}} answered), {{[0-9]+}} writes
# CHECK: PASS
